# Drill-down detail hero — no white frame

Every "one level inside" detail view — reached by clicking `View` on a table
row to open a page showing a header/hero (icon + title + badges/subtext,
optionally a row of `CountCard`s) followed by another table — must have its
back button and hero section sit **directly on the gray canvas**, with no
wrapping `border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white` card around them.

Only two things are allowed their own white background:

1. Each individual `CountCard` (already self-contained via `CountCard.jsx`).
2. The actual data table below the hero (its own `border border-gray-200
   rounded-lg bg-white` wrapper, or the shared `SectionCard`).

```jsx
// Bad — hero + CountCards wrapped in one big white card
<div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white p-5">
  <div className="flex items-center gap-3">{icon}<h2>{title}</h2></div>
  <div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-3 mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
    {kpis.map(k => <CountCard key={k.label} {...k} />)}
  </div>
</div>

// Good — header on canvas, CountCards in their own row, no shared wrapper
<div className="flex items-center gap-3">{icon}<h2>{title}</h2></div>
<div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-3">
  {kpis.map(k => <CountCard key={k.label} {...k} />)}
</div>
```

- Icon/avatar next to the title stays vertically centered with the title
  text: use `items-center` on the header row's flex container (not
  `items-start`).
- Reference implementations: `TopicDetailContent` / `DomainDetailContent` in
  `AiSearchPerformanceDashboard.jsx`, the crawled-page/found-resource detail
  views in `SiteHealthDashboard.jsx`, `SourceAnswersDetailView` in
  `SourceInventoryContent.jsx`, and `PromptDetailView` in
  `PromptTrackingDashboard.jsx`.

## Before finishing any new drill-down view

- [ ] Back button + hero sit on the canvas — no `bg-white` wrapper around them.
- [ ] Any KPI/count cards are a plain `grid`, not nested inside a shared white card.
- [ ] Icon/avatar is vertically centered with the title (`items-center`).
- [ ] Only the table (and each `CountCard` individually) has its own white
  bordered box.
